data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Dispatch d002 — greet, tested: summary\\n\\n## What I did\\n\\n- Created `src/greet.py` defining `greet(name)`, which returns `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`.\\n- Created `tests/test_greet.py` (unittest) with two test cases:\\n  - `greet(\\\"Ada\\\") == \\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"` (normal name)\\n  - `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"` (empty string)\\n- The test file prepends `../src` to `sys.path` so `src/greet.py` imports cleanly\\n  while staying at exactly `src/greet.py`.\\n\\n## Test result\\n\\nRan from the repository root (`~/subject`):\\n\\n    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n\\nOutput: `Ran 2 tests in 0.000s — OK`, exit code **0**.\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\n- Branch: `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`\\n- Commit: `5e91df8 Add greet module with unittest coverage` (2 files, 21 insertions)\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Nothing blocked; all acceptance criteria met.\\n\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_10","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1788671469,"id":"chatcmpl-2de354bab1e34fa2af2cdf2fdd9ce18a","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

